WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
A turban over uncut hair.

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:04.230
A kara on the wrist.

3
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.210
A kirpan at the side.

4
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.180
For many Sikhs, identity is visible.

5
00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.580
It cannot simply be kept private.

6
00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:15.490
And in Britain, some Sikhs marry
partners from outside the faith.

7
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.500
So who decides what is allowed: at school,

8
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:20.430
at work, at a wedding?

9
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.700
In this mission, you'll set the five
articles of faith beside British law,

10
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:25.930
one by one.

11
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:31.320
Then you'll weigh up a hard question: can
Sikh identity survive in a secular country

12
00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:32.940
without compromise?

13
00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:37.220
Your mission: find out who decides
what a Sikh in Britain may wear,

14
00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.610
carry and marry.
